814: \begin{definition}[\(k\)-rational point]\leanok
815:   \label{def:has_rational_point}
816:   \lean{AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.HasRationalPoint}
817:   The predicate \(\mathrm{HasRationalPoint}(C)\) asserts that the structural
818:   morphism \(C \to \Spec k\) admits a section
819:   \(\sigma : \Spec k \to C\), i.e.\ that \(C\) has a \(k\)-rational point.
820:   This is the standing hypothesis of the chapter (see
821:   \cref{sec:fga_pic_setup}): by Kleiman \S 2, Thm.~2.5, it makes the plain
822:   relative Picard functor \(\Pic^\sharp_{C/k}\) coincide with its \'etale
823:   (and fppf) sheafification, so representability can be stated against
824:   \cref{def:rel_pic_sharp} directly. For a pointed curve \((C,P)\), the
825:   pointing \(P\) supplies this section.
826: \end{definition}
